WHAT THIS COVERS
----------------
`LICENSE` (MIT) speaks about the Software. It says nothing about a database right,
which would leave the data in this repository -- the part a reader is most likely to
reuse -- with unstated terms. This file states them, by path:

    data/raw/indata-synthetic.xlsx     the synthetic model instance
    data/raw/fitted_parameters.json    the fitted aggregate parameters it is drawn from
    results/tables/**                  the committed cleaned output
    results/figures/**                 the reproducible figures
    figures/**                         the published figures from the paper
    docs/**                            the synthetic-data findings

Everything else -- all Python source under `src/`, `scripts/` and `tests/`, the
notebooks under `notebooks/`, and the archived originals under `archive/` and
`model-gams/` -- is covered by `LICENSE` (MIT).

CHOOSING NOTHING IS CHOOSING
----------------------------
Zenodo's licence field is required and defaults to CC-BY, so an unstated choice
becomes a stated one at deposit. This file makes the choice deliberately rather than
letting the deposit form make it.

CC BY rather than CC0 because these tables are the evidence behind a published
paper: attribution is the point, and citation norms alone have not proved enough.

WHAT IS NOT HERE, AND IS NOT LICENSED BY THIS FILE
--------------------------------------------------
The original model inputs derive from Pecan Street household data and are NOT
distributed in this repository. Nothing in this file grants any right to them. The
shipped instance is sampled from fitted aggregate parameters rather than perturbed
from the originals, so it does not reproduce any household series.

